ct crew cooperation and professional communication. B has strong reliability and stress but uncooperative. D has strong responsibility and problem solving but arrogance and weak leadership. A has strong anticipation and technical but unorganized.\n\nProbably C is best overall despite communication issues? But communication is critical. Egocentric and difficulty communicating ideas could be serious. B's uncooperative also serious. D's arrogance also serious. A's unorganized could affect reliability.\n\nWe might need more info on communication for B and D. Could ask other agents. But we need to make a contribution now. We can state provisional recommendation maybe Candidate C, but note concerns. Or we could hold off and ask for more info. However we must produce a public message with a vote. The instruction says we must state or clearly imply current hiring recommendation. So we need to vote now.\n\nGiven the evidence, I think Candidate C has strongest overall fit: reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere. Communication difficulty is a concern but may be mitigated. Others have bigger issues (uncooperative, arrogance, unorganized). So I will vote Candidate C.\n\nProvide argument referencing facts: reliability 100%, correct decisions quickly, positive crew atmosphere, but note communication difficulty and egocentric as concerns.\n\nLet's produce public message."}
